# Dialogic 2 timeline — Henrietta at the Archive Door
# Game One, opening sequence. Roland has just arrived at the Loremaster's Archive.
# #
# CONTEXT (from lore/GAME1_PART1.md):
#   Henrietta has been quietly compiling genealogical research she doesn't fully
#   understand. She knows someone has been asking about the restricted records —
#   someone she doesn't recognise. She has prepared a duplicate of her notes.
#   She presses it into Roland's coat at the door and doesn't explain why.
#   Within twenty-four hours she will be dead.
# #
# FORMAT:
#   This file uses Dialogic 2's text timeline syntax.
#   Each line is: CharacterDisplayName: "Spoken text."
#   The display name must match exactly what you set in the Dialogic
#   Characters editor (see design/DIALOGIC_SETUP.md, Step 3).
#   Open this file in the Dialogic timeline editor (double-click in FileSystem)
#   to view and edit it visually, or to fix any character-link errors.

Henrietta: "Don't come inside. Stay at the door."

Roland: "Your message said urgent."

Henrietta: "Eleven pieces of research I shouldn't have pulled. Someone else was asking for them today — someone I don't know."

Henrietta: "Take this. It's a copy — the originals stay here. Don't let anyone see it until you're out of Aldenholt."

Roland: "Henrietta, what have you found?"

Henrietta: "Nothing I can explain at a door in the dark. Go. East gate, not the main road."

Henrietta: "And Roland — be careful who you trust at the Iron Chalice."